The input is a data cube of dimensions MxQxN. The first dimension is range, or fast time. The second dimension is angle, or channels. The third dimension is Doppler, or slow time. 

If you set the Output Slice parameter to 'Angle-Doppler', the output is of dimension QxN. If you set the Output Slice parameter to 'Range-Doppler', the output is of dimension MxN. If you set the Output Slice parameter to 'Range-angle', the output is of dimension MxQ.</block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Cube Slicer</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/Cube Slicer</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>0</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>230  132  360  188</block_position><block_icon>Cube@20@Slicer.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>signal.in_signal:2,signal.out_signal:1</port_domains><block_type>Selector</block_type><block_reference></block_reference></block_node></library>